{"The blacklist comparison lowercases the blacklisted emails but not the incoming `guest` email. A user can bypass the blacklist by submitting an email with different casing (e.g., `Blocked@example.com`).": 0.9893137812614441, "The permission check uses `&&` (AND) instead of `||` (OR). This requires the user to be both a team admin and a team owner simultaneously, which is almost never true. A team admin or team owner should each independently have permission to add guests.": 0.9847822785377502, "`sendAddGuestsEmails` is called with the raw `guests` input instead of `uniqueGuests`. This means notification emails may be sent for guests who were already attendees or were filtered out by the blacklist.": 0.9963721036911011, "`uniqueGuests` only filters against existing booking attendees and the blacklist, but does not deduplicate the input `guests` array itself. Submitting the same email twice in the request will create duplicate attendee records.": 0.9766495227813721, "Seat bookings need seat-level scoping, but this new action updates by `bookingId` only. On seats events it can add guests to the shared booking instead of the current seat.": 0.8257190585136414, "Spread `props` before the fixed template props, otherwise callers can override this email's subject, title, and header.": 0.9863459467887878}